TABLE COMMANDS

Table commands in SQL are used to create, modify, rename, and remove the structure of tables within a database.

Commands	and What it does

🟢 CREATE TABLE:     Creates a new table and defines its structure
🟡 ALTER TABLE:   	  Modifies the structure of an existing table
🔵 RENAME TABLE:     Changes the name of an existing table
🟠 TRUNCATE TABLE	:   Removes all records while keeping the table structure
🔴 DROP TABLE:    	  Permanently removes the table and its structure


🟢 CREATE TABLE

Used to create a new table by defining its:

Columns
Data types
Constraints
Relationships

🟡 ALTER TABLE

Used to change the structure of an existing table.

It can be used to:

Add columns
Modify columns
Rename columns
Remove columns
Add constraints
Remove constraints

🔵 RENAME TABLE

Used to change the name of an existing table without changing its data or overall structure.

🟠 TRUNCATE TABLE

Used to remove all records from a table while keeping the table itself and its structure.

Data is removed → Structure remains.

🔴 DROP TABLE

Used to permanently remove an entire table, including its structure and stored data.

Table + Data + Structure → Removed.
